===== Verify OpenWrt installation =====
   * Telnet to 192.168.1.1 on standard port(23)
   * If it does not work try:
     1) Telnet to 10.10.12.72 (alt. 192.168.1.1) on port 9000 to get Redboot prompt
<code>RedBoot> fis load -l vmlinux.bin.l7
RedBoot> go 0x80041000 </code>

2) Now you can see Open Wrt promt.
<code>root@OpenWrt:/# </code>
     
3) Thus you have to correct booting procedure. Reboot device
<code>Telnet to 10.10.12.72
RedBoot> fconfig -l 
RedBoot> fconfig boot_script_data</code>

Enter following:

<code>fis load -l vmlinux.bin.l7
go 0x80041000
</code>

Save and reboot.

